boothb                package:AA                     R Documentation

Data on Responses to Analgesic

Description:

     The 'boothb' data frame has 18 rows and 2 columns.

     This data set contains the responses for two groups of subjects to
     a  given analgesic: the numbers reported are the differences in
     pain response for each subject, before and after treatment.

Usage:

     data(boothb)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'y' the differences in pain response for each subject, before and 
          after use of the analgesic;

     'Group' the group indicator (1/0) for each subject;

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Petrie, A. (1978).  _Individuality in Pain and Suffering_ (2nd 
     Ed.).  University of Chicago Press, Chigago.  Page 54.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 7.8.

     Booth, J.G. and Butler, R.W. (1990).  Randomization distributions 
     and saddlepoint approximations in generalized linear models.  
     _Biometrika_, *77*, 787-796.

Examples:

     data(boothb)
     plot(y ~ factor(Group), data = boothb, xlab = "group", 
          ylab = "differences in pain response")
